\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Grouped success counts for the 24-case primary startup matrix. Each row corresponds to one design and each column group to one factor family. Every row is identical: the entire five-design pack is tied at $17/24$ startups. This figure is intentionally a null result. It shows that the global startup envelope in the chosen matrix is unchanged by adding packet gating, by joining both inputs, or by changing the pre-handoff selector law.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:primary}{{3}{12}{Grouped success counts for the 24-case primary startup matrix. Each row corresponds to one design and each column group to one factor family. Every row is identical: the entire five-design pack is tied at $17/24$ startups. This figure is intentionally a null result. It shows that the global startup envelope in the chosen matrix is unchanged by adding packet gating, by joining both inputs, or by changing the pre-handoff selector law.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
